            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for a hut, then the Gujarati for to lay waste."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: તણાવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તણાવું — taṇāvũ — \"to be swept away\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પૂરમાં અમારી ગાય તણાઈ ગઈ. pūrmā̃ amārī gāy taṇāī gaī. Our cow was swept away in the flood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): તે ઝૂંપડું તણાઈ ગયું, te jhū̃pḍũ taṇāī gayũ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તણાવું (taṇāvũ) goes back to Sanskrit tanṓti, \"stretches\", and CDIAL lists the Gujarati verb, \"to be dragged\" (CDIAL 5659): a flood drags things along with it. તણાઈ ગયું, it was swept away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
